{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d",
		"name": "module-manager",
		"description": "Postman collection for the Module Manager (MM) Go backend.\n\nBase URL is driven by the `baseUrl` collection variable (default: http://localhost:8778, see `.env` -> `Port`).\n\nTypical flow:\n1. `Health Check` – verify the server is up.\n2. `Set Path` – point MM at the parent folder containing your Node.js projects.\n3. `Scan Main Folder` – list detected projects (supports `limit` / `offset` pagination); results are cached server-side and build the project index.\n4. `Get Project By Id` – fetch a single project using an `id` returned by the scan.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Health",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Health Check",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/healthz",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "healthz"]
						},
						"description": "`GET /api/healthz` → `handlers.Health`\n\nSimple liveness probe. Returns server time (IST zone, format `YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss`) and a fixed message."
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "200 - Server healthy",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "GET",
								"header": [],
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/healthz",
									"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
									"path": ["api", "healthz"]
								}
							},
							"status": "OK",
							"code": 200,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"cookie": [],
							"body": "{\n    \"success\": true,\n    \"current_time\": \"2026-08-26 12:00:00\",\n    \"message\": \"server is working fine\"\n}"
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "API",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Set Path",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"path\": \"C:\\\\Programming\\\\projects\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/set-path",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "set-path"]
						},
						"description": "`POST /api/set-path` → `handlers.SetPath`\n\nSets the parent folder that subsequent scans will read from. The path is stored in memory (server state) and is not persisted across restarts.\n\nErrors (400):\n- `Invalid JSON` – malformed request body.\n- `path cannot be empty` – missing/blank `path` field.\n\nSuccess (200):\n- Standard envelope returned by `utils.JsonResponse`: `message` = `path is set`, `data.path` echoes the stored path."
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "201 - Path accepted",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json"
									}
								],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"path\": \"C:\\\\Programming\\\\projects\"\n}",
									"options": {
										"raw": {
											"language": "json"
										}
									}
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/set-path",
									"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
									"path": ["api", "set-path"]
								}
							},
							"status": "Created",
							"code": 201,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"cookie": [],
							"body": "{}"
						},
						{
							"name": "400 - Empty path",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json"
									}
								],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n    \"path\": \"\"\n}",
									"options": {
										"raw": {
											"language": "json"
										}
									}
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/set-path",
									"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
									"path": ["api", "set-path"]
								}
							},
							"status": "Bad Request",
							"code": 400,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "text",
							"header": [],
							"cookie": [],
							"body": "path cannot be empty"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Scan Main Folder",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/folders/scan?limit=20&offset=0",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "folders", "scan"],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "limit",
									"value": "20",
									"description": "Max number of directory entries to return. Default: 20. Must be > 0."
								},
								{
									"key": "offset",
									"value": "0",
									"description": "Number of directory entries to skip before returning. Default: 0. Must be >= 0."
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "`POST /api/folders/scan` → `handlers.ScanFolder`\n\nScans the parent folder previously set via `/api/set-path`, reads its immediate subdirectories and returns basic info for each project (id, name, path, recursive size).\n\nQuery params:\n- `limit` (optional, default 20)\n- `offset` (optional, default 0)\n\nErrors (400):\n- `invalid limit` / `invalid offset` – non-numeric or out-of-range values.\n- `folder does not exist.` / `path is not a directory/folder.` – bad stored path.\n\nCall `Set Path` first, otherwise no folder is configured."
					},
					"response": [
						{
							"name": "201 - Scan result",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [],
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/folders/scan?limit=20&offset=0",
									"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
									"path": ["api", "folders", "scan"],
									"query": [
										{
											"key": "limit",
											"value": "20"
										},
										{
											"key": "offset",
											"value": "0"
										}
									]
								}
							},
							"status": "Created",
							"code": 201,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
							"header": [
								{
									"key": "Content-Type",
									"value": "application/json"
								}
							],
							"cookie": [],
							"body": "{\n    \"path\": \"C:\\\\Programming\\\\projects\",\n    \"total_projects\": 2,\n    \"total_size\": 123456789,\n    \"projects\": [\n        {\n            \"id\": \"0my-app\",\n            \"name\": \"my-app\",\n            \"path\": \"C:\\\\Programming\\\\projects\\\\my-app\",\n            \"is_dir\": true,\n            \"total_size\": 61728394\n        },\n        {\n            \"id\": \"1my-api\",\n            \"name\": \"my-api\",\n            \"path\": \"C:\\\\Programming\\\\projects\\\\my-api\",\n            \"is_dir\": true,\n            \"total_size\": 61728395\n        }\n    ]\n}"
						},
						{
							"name": "400 - Invalid limit",
							"originalRequest": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [],
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/folders/scan?limit=-1&offset=0",
									"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
									"path": ["api", "folders", "scan"],
									"query": [
										{
											"key": "limit",
											"value": "-1"
										},
										{
											"key": "offset",
											"value": "0"
										}
									]
								}
							},
							"status": "Bad Request",
							"code": 400,
							"_postman_previewlanguage": "text",
							"header": [],
